<title>FRANCE: ABSat aims at 75,000 subscribers at end 1997.</title>
<headline>ABSat aims at 75,000 subscribers at end 1997.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABSat, the digital satellite television service of AB Productions, aims to have about 75,000 susbcribers at the end of the year against about 5,000 now, as the result of a commercial campaign.</p>
<p>A spokesman for ABSat said &quot;We have an 80 percent chance of arriving at 50,000 subscribers.&quot;</p>
<p>Rival TPS says it has 110,000 subscribers while Canalsatellite has 300,000 subscribers to its digital service.</p>
<p>AB Productions, listed in New York, is scheduled to announce its 1996 results on Monday.</p>
<p>But it may delay this due to a fire which ravaged the ABSat building in La Plaine Saint-Denis, near Paris, on Thursday.</p>
</text>
